        "raw": "<p>Played a game tonight that included Chrono-Ranger and Haka against Miss Information. &nbsp;She had two Diversions (that were targets) out early. &nbsp;Haka got out Savage Mana and enough damage was done to allow him to deal the finishing blows to each target and put it under Savage Mana.</p><p>First: &nbsp;Chrono-Ranger had By Any Means (with text of &quot;When that target leaves play, destroy this card.&quot;) on one of the targets. &nbsp;When Haka destroyed that target and put it under Savage Mana, I destroyed By Any Means. &nbsp;Going back through some recent threads on here, I believe that was incorrect because while the target was destroyed, it did not leave play since it went under Savage Mana. &nbsp;I wasn&#39;t horribly concerned about that one because By Any Means would&#39;ve just hung out in limbo for two turns, as Jim&#39;s Hat came out next turn and would&#39;ve allowed the destruction of By Any Means the turn after that. &nbsp;I just wanted to confirm that I&#39;d misplayed that, and that By Any Means should not have been destroyed when the Diversion target was destroyed and put under Savage Mana.</p><p>Second: &nbsp;Because of Guise&#39; card copying abilities, I believe we know that &quot;card text&quot; doesn&#39;t include keywords (though I can&#39;t find the quote to cite it). &nbsp;Cards under cards don&#39;t have any text, but they do retain the type of card they are (Hero, Villain, or Environment.) &nbsp;Do they retain their keywords? &nbsp;Miss Information&#39;s front side says &quot;At the end of the Villain turn, destroy X Hero Ongoing or Equipment cards, where X = the number of Diversion cards in play.&quot; &nbsp;For the two Diversion cards that were targets that were destroyed and put under Savage Mana, they were technically still &quot;in play&quot;, and were they still Diversion cards that would have had Miss Information destroying 2 Hero Ongoing or Equipment cards each turn?<br /><br />A possibly more common example of the second scenario would be Haka + Savage Mana vs. Voss + Minions. &nbsp;If Haka destroys a bunch of Minions and puts them under Savage Mana, but they&#39;re still considered &quot;in play&quot;, are they also still considered &quot;Minion&quot; cards which would count toward Voss&#39; win condition and damage reduction?</p>",
